Signing and verifying before the fix:

// auth/tokens.ts
signAccess(userId: string): string {
  const now = Date.now();
  return this.hs256.sign({ sub: userId, iat: Math.floor(now / 1000), exp: now + 15 * 60 * 1000,
                          iss: "https://api.codedev.test", aud: "codedev-web" });
}

// auth/jwt.guard.ts (after the signature check passed)
if (payload.exp <= Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000)) throw new UnauthorizedException("token_expired");

Decoded payload of a token issued at 2026-10-26 09:00:00 UTC:
{"sub":"u_1042","iat":1793005200,"exp":1793006100000,"iss":"https://api.codedev.test","aud":"codedev-web"}

Statement: "Tokens issued by this code pass the expiry check for tens of thousands of years, and the signature check cannot catch it, because the API itself signed the wrong exp."
